            "content": {
                "image_source": {
                    "path": "images/fd1440b787fc68a51cd90d237d974157958e1fcba9737204bf8db8ea55088334.jpg"
                },
                "content": "",
                "chart_caption": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "FiG. 1. Critical pitting potentials of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "1 8 \\% \\mathbf { C r } ,"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "10%Ni, Re stainless steels in 0·1N NaCl."
                    }
                ],
                "chart_footnote": []
            },
            "bbox": [
                324,
                305,
                628,
                518
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": []
            },
            "bbox": [
                189,
                570,
                783,
                723
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Critical pitting potentials in 0·1N NaCl at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 \\mathrm { ^ \\circ C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "shown in Fig. 1 indicate that alloyed Re, like alloyed "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { M } \\circ ,"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "shifts the critical potential in the noble direction corresponding to an increased resistance to pitting corrosion. Similar to alloyed "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { M o } ,"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "the shift at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\boldsymbol { \\mathfrak { O } } ^ { \\circ } \\mathbf { C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "is in the opposite or more active direction. The 75mV decrease at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "{ \\boldsymbol { 0 } } ^ { \\circ } { \\bf C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "on adding "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "1 { \\cdot } 8 4 \\% \\mathsf { R e }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(0.55at.%), however, is less than the corresponding decrease of almost 500mV on adding 1·8%Mo (1·05at.%)."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                191,
                722,
                783,
                814
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The observed effects in 0·1N NaBr (Fig. 2) at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 \\mathrm { { ^ \\circ C } }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "are somewhat different fiom those for the Mo stainless steels in that alloyed Re increases the critical pitting potential whereas alloyed Mo decreases it. Also at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } { \\bf C } , 1 { \\cdot } 8 4 \\% { \\bf R e }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "causes a slight shift of critical potential of 30mV in the active direction whereas "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 { \\cdot } 5 \\% \\mathbf { M } \\mathbf { o }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "produces a change of over"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                191,
                814,
                785,
                876
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "content": {
                "page_number_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "354"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                191,
                150,
                216,
                161
            ]
        },
        {
