            ]
        }
    ],
    [
        {
            "type": "chart",
            "content": {
                "image_source": {
                    "path": "images/b5f34e958cbf10c126b9a54c01144b80455a81f6b60a6fd0880471eb82179078.jpg"
                },
                "content": "",
                "chart_caption": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "FiG. 2. Critical pitting potentials of "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "1 8 \\% \\mathrm { { C r } , 1 0 \\% N i }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Re stainless steels in0·1N NaBr."
                    }
                ],
                "chart_footnote": []
            },
            "bbox": [
                336,
                189,
                642,
                404
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "100mV in the same direction. Stainless steels of the 18-8 variety at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 \\mathrm { ^ \\circ C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "are more resistant to pitting in NaBr than in "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\bf N a C l"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "but the critical potentials indicate that the alloy containing "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "1 { \\cdot } 8 \\% 8 e"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "is almost equally resistant in either medium. "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "\\mathbf { A t 0 ^ { \\circ } C } ,"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "resistance is better in chlorides than in bromides whether or not the alloys contain Re."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                191,
                439,
                782,
                501
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Results requiring explanation are (1) the much more noble critical potential for "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 \\text{‰}"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "stainless steel at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 ^ { \\circ }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "compared to "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "{ 2 5 \\mathrm { ‰} }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in 0·1N NaCl. On the other hand in 0·1N NaBr, the less noble critical potential at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "{ \\boldsymbol { 0 } } ^ { \\circ } { \\bf C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "than at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 \\mathrm { ^ \\circ C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "(2) The increase of critical potential brought about by alloyed Re at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "2 5 \\mathrm { ‰}"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "but the decrease at "
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "equation_inline",
                        "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathbf { C }"
                    },
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "in either 0·1N NaCl or 0·1N NaBr. (3) The greater sensitivity to temperature of the Mo- compared to the Re-stainless steels. As is discussed in the earlier reference¹ these effects are not readily explained by temperature coefficients of diffusion through a supposed oxide film. The effect of temperature is more likely due to an alteration of double layer structure caused by a temperature-dependent hydration of the relevant ions and of the passive film itself, thereby affecting competitive adsorption of anions with adsorbed oxygen of the passive film for sites on the metal surface."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
